# Plugin development

Read `examples/AGENTS.md` for the plugin authoring instructions and `docs/plugins.md`
for the host contract, trust policy and deployment workflow.

- Use the public `Vestigo.Extensibility` contracts; independent plugins reference
  the contracts NuGet, never `Vestigo.Server` or private host implementations.
- Keep plugin loading and module activation explicitly opt-in. Use the existing
  MCP endpoint, DI and authenticated HTTP route groups; no anonymous plugin routes.
- Publish the full dependency graph and validate published artifacts, shared type
  identity, tool names and disabled/authenticated behavior. Do not weaken ACLs,
  path checks, trust pins or API compatibility checks to make integration pass.
- Keep corporate code and binaries out of the public host and installer. Plugins
  run with service privileges; dependency isolation is not a security sandbox.

The portable instructions in `examples/AGENTS.md` can also be copied into a separate
plugin repository. Repository-wide branch, interop and documentation rules still
apply to contributions in this checkout.
